# Grist 1.7.18 (image gristlabs/grist:1.7.18) environment schema
# (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# Source: grep of `process.env.X` and of the `appSettings` reader form
# (`.readString/.requireString/.readBool/.requireInt({ envVar: "X" })`) across
# app/ and stubs/ at grist-core v1.7.18, plus the image defaults baked into
# the release Dockerfile's own `ENV` block. Test-only, hosted-Grist-only
# (Stripe / Help Scout / Discourse / GRIST_HOSTED*) and build-time-only
# (GRIST_EDITION, GRIST_SKIP_EXT_AUTOSETUP, consumed by `yarn install`, not by
# the server) variables are deliberately left out.
#
# Cross-checked against the README "Environment variables" table shipped in
# the same tag. The table is accurate except:
#   * it calls the attachment-size hint `GRIST_ATTACHMENT_THRESHOLD_MB`; the
#     code only ever reads `GRIST_ATTACHMENTS_THRESHOLD_MB`
#     (app/server/lib/GranularAccess.ts). The documented spelling does nothing.
#   * it says `GRIST_EXTERNAL_ATTACHMENTS_MODE` defaults to "none" and that
#     "none" turns the feature off. In 1.7.18 the code default is "snapshots"
#     (app/server/lib/AttachmentStoreProvider.ts) and the literal string
#     "none" is NOT a recognised value: it falls through to
#     `throw new UnsupportedExternalAttachmentsMode(...)`. Only "snapshots"
#     and "test" are accepted.
#   * it documents `HOME_PORT`, which only exists in app/server/devServerMain.ts
#     (the source dev entrypoint). The container runs
#     `_build/stubs/app/server/server.js`, which reads `PORT` and defaults to
#     8484. `GRIST_PORT` belongs to the separate MergedServer entrypoint and
#     is not on the container's path either.
#   * it lists `GRIST_APP_ROOT`, which nothing in app/ or stubs/ reads at this
#     tag.
#
# SECURITY, stated plainly:
#   * GRIST_SESSION_SECRET is the key every session cookie is signed with.
#     app/server/lib/ICreate.ts falls back to a HARD-CODED default when it is
#     unset, and that default is public in the source tree. An unset secret
#     means anyone can forge a session cookie for any user, including the
#     install owner. The Admin Panel warns about exactly this. It must be set
#     and it must be secret.
#   * The compose sets no OIDC/SAML/forward-auth provider, so Grist falls back
#     to app/server/lib/MinimalLogin.ts: "Sign in" logs the visitor in as
#     GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL with no password prompt at all.
#     GRIST_FORCE_LOGIN="true" only requires that the visitor performs that
#     click. Treat this install as open to anyone who can reach it until a
#     real identity provider (GRIST_OIDC_* / GRIST_SAML_* / forward auth) is
#     configured, or until the network in front of it authenticates.
#   * GRIST_SINGLE_USER=1 makes Authorizer.ts skip document authorization
#     entirely (DocManager logs "not using authorization"). GRIST_IGNORE_SESSION
#     turns off session-based auth so an upstream proxy header is the only
#     identity. Both are single-tenant / trusted-network switches; either one
#     on a reachable server means no access control.
#
# The compose prompts for GRIST_URL, GRIST_SESSION_SECRET and
# GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL and threads them, unchanged, into APP_HOME_URL and the
# container's own GRIST_SESSION_SECRET / GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL.
#
# First run (behaviour new since 1.7.13/1.7.15, not present at the previously
# pinned 1.7.4): a fresh install writes GRIST_IN_SERVICE="false" and a random
# GRIST_BOOT_KEY into its own home database and stays "out of service" until an
# operator visits /boot with that key and finishes Quick setup. The key is
# printed in the container logs. Setting GRIST_IN_SERVICE=true below skips the
# gate.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("Grist environment variables (v1.7.18 README)", https://github.com/gristlabs/grist-core/blob/v1.7.18/README.md#environment-variables)
# ---

# ─── Core ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Platform prompt key for this instance's public URL; threaded unchanged into
# APP_HOME_URL below. Every link, redirect and OAuth callback Grist builds
# starts from it.
# @required
# @type=url
# @docs("Self-managed Grist", https://support.getgrist.com/self-managed/)
GRIST_URL=

# URL prefix the home server and doc workers use to address themselves and
# each other. Set by the compose from GRIST_URL. Wrong here means broken
# redirects and custom-widget frames that never load.
# @required
# @type=url
APP_HOME_URL=${GRIST_URL}

# Internal-network twin of APP_HOME_URL, for server-to-server calls that
# should not leave the Docker network. Defaults to APP_HOME_URL.
# @type=url
APP_HOME_INTERNAL_URL=

# Public URL of this doc worker, in a multi-server deployment. A single
# container does not need it, and setting it together with GRIST_FLEET is
# refused at startup.
# @type=url
APP_DOC_URL=

# Internal-network twin of APP_DOC_URL. Defaults to APP_DOC_URL; if both are
# unset an address is derived from GRIST_HOST or from the interface used to
# reach Redis.
# @type=url
APP_DOC_INTERNAL_URL=

# URL prefix static assets are served from, if you front them with a CDN.
# Empty serves them from the app itself.
APP_STATIC_URL=

# Origin that untrusted plugin/custom-widget content is served from, so its
# cookies are separated from the app's. Empty keeps widgets on the app origin
# (see GRIST_UNTRUSTED_PORT for the port-based alternative).
APP_UNTRUSTED_URL=

# Port the container's server (stubs/app/server/server.ts) listens on. The
# compose exposes 8484 with no override, so this is that port's twin: change
# it and the exposed port stops matching.
# @type=port
PORT=8484

# Address to bind. The image bakes 0.0.0.0 so the container network can reach
# it; unset would bind localhost only. It also decides the address this server
# publishes to its peers.
GRIST_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Serve the home server, the doc worker and static assets on ONE port. Baked
# into the image; a single-container deployment needs it.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SINGLE_PORT=true

# Address home server and doc workers on the same protocol-host-port as the
# top-level page instead of on separate hostnames. Baked into the image. The
# Host header must be trustworthy, which behind otterdeploy's proxy it is.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SERVE_SAME_ORIGIN=true

# Encode the org in the URL path (/o/docs/...) rather than as a subdomain.
# Baked into the image; this is what makes a single-hostname deployment work.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ORG_IN_PATH=true

# Pins every browser to one org "domain", i.e. single-team mode. The compose
# sets "docs", which is the shape that makes sense for one server: no site
# picker, no personal-org sprawl.
GRIST_SINGLE_ORG=docs

# Base domain that hosted Grist serves org subdomains of. Defaults to
# "getgrist.com" and is irrelevant while GRIST_ORG_IN_PATH is on.
GRIST_DOMAIN=

# Accept more than one base domain by trusting the Host header. Only turn on
# behind a proxy that validates Host itself.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ADAPT_DOMAIN=

# For org subdomains of the form o-*, expect/produce o-${GRIST_ID_PREFIX}*.
GRIST_ID_PREFIX=

# Which server roles this process runs. Defaults to "home,docs,static";
# "app" is the fourth option. One container wants the default.
GRIST_SERVERS=

# Appended to the HTML <title>. Defaults to " - Grist"; set to the literal
# _blank for no suffix at all.
GRIST_PAGE_TITLE_SUFFIX=

# Fallback locale when the browser's own locale is not supported. Must match a
# code in app/common/LocaleCodes.ts. Defaults to en-US.
GRIST_DEFAULT_LOCALE=

# Offer every translation, not only the ones marked complete enough.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_OFFER_ALL_LANGUAGES=

# ─── Sessions and secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The key every Grist session cookie is signed with. Platform prompt key,
# generated once and threaded unchanged into the container. If it is empty,
# app/server/lib/ICreate.ts silently uses a hard-coded default that is public
# in the upstream source, and anyone who knows it can forge a session for any
# account on this server, including the install owner. Rotating it logs
# everyone out, which is the correct response to a leak.
# @required
# @sensitive
GRIST_SESSION_SECRET=${GRIST_SESSION_SECRET}

# Name of the session cookie. The image bakes "grist_core"; the code's own
# default (app/server/lib/gristSessions.ts) is "grist_sid". Changing it
# invalidates existing sessions.
GRIST_SESSION_COOKIE=grist_core

# Domain the session cookie is scoped to. Empty falls back to GRIST_DOMAIN.
# Only widen this if you deliberately share sessions across subdomains.
GRIST_SESSION_DOMAIN=

# Session cookie lifetime in milliseconds; defaults to 90 days. The literal
# "none" makes it a browser-session cookie that dies when the browser closes.
COOKIE_MAX_AGE=

# Redis URL for shared browser sessions and DB query caching. Required only if
# you run more than one Grist container; a single container keeps sessions in
# SQLite. Contains the password when one is set.
# @sensitive
REDIS_URL=

# ─── Accounts and access ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("Logins (v1.7.18 README)", https://github.com/gristlabs/grist-core/blob/v1.7.18/README.md#logins)

# The account that owns this installation. Platform prompt key, threaded
# unchanged into the container. It is also the identity the fallback login
# system hands out: with no OIDC/SAML/forward-auth configured, clicking "Sign
# in" logs the visitor in as this address with no password
# (app/server/lib/MinimalLogin.ts). Leave the server unreachable, or configure
# a real identity provider, before treating it as private.
# @required
# @type=email
GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL=${GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL}

# Overrides which email counts as the installation admin. Checked first;
# GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL, then support@getgrist.com, are the fallbacks
# (app/server/lib/InstallAdmin.ts).
# @type=email
GRIST_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# Grants an account "support" powers, chiefly listing shared sites/docs to
# everyone. Defaults to support@getgrist.com, which nobody can log in as here.
# @type=email
GRIST_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# Block all anonymous access: every page, including publicly shared documents,
# requires a signed-in user first. The compose sets "true". Note this makes
# people sign in, it does not by itself make signing in hard (see
# GRIST_DEFAULT_EMAIL above).
# @type=boolean
GRIST_FORCE_LOGIN=true

# When "false", anonymous visitors are denied the home page (documents shared
# with anyone can still be opened). Defaults to true, unless
# GRIST_ORG_CREATION_ANYONE is false. Redundant while GRIST_FORCE_LOGIN is on.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ANON_PLAYGROUND=

# When "false", signing up no longer creates a personal org for the new user.
# Defaults to true, unless GRIST_ORG_CREATION_ANYONE is false.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_PERSONAL_ORGS=

# When "false", non-admins cannot create new team sites, and the defaults of
# GRIST_ANON_PLAYGROUND and GRIST_PERSONAL_ORGS flip to false with it.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ORG_CREATION_ANYONE=

# Show the UI affordances for anonymous access. Off by default.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SUPPORT_ANON=

# List publicly shared sites to anonymous users. Defaults to false.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_LIST_PUBLIC_SITES=

# DANGEROUS. "1" makes app/server/lib/Authorizer.ts skip document
# authorization completely. DocManager logs "not using authorization" and
# every document is open to whoever asks. Intended for a desktop/local
# single-user run, never for a server anyone else can reach.
GRIST_SINGLE_USER=

# DANGEROUS unless paired with forward auth. Stops Grist using its session for
# authentication (app/server/lib/ForwardAuthLogin.ts), so the identity comes
# from a proxy-set header on every request. Without such a proxy in front,
# nothing authenticates the request at all. Defaults to false.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_IGNORE_SESSION=

# Pins which login system to use instead of letting Grist pick the first
# configured one (oidc, saml, forward-auth, minimal).
GRIST_LOGIN_SYSTEM_TYPE=

# ─── First-run setup gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("First-run setup", https://support.getgrist.com/install/first-run-setup/)

# "true" puts the server straight into service and skips the Quick setup gate.
# A brand-new install stores "false" in its own home database instead, so it
# stays administrative-only until an operator completes /boot + Quick setup.
# Existing installs are already in service.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_IN_SERVICE=

# Key that signs you in as the installation admin at /boot. New installs
# generate a random one and print it at startup; set this only to choose your
# own. Anyone with this value becomes install admin, so treat it as a
# password, and prefer reading the generated one out of the container logs.
# @sensitive
GRIST_BOOT_KEY=

# ─── Home database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The home DB holds users, orgs, workspaces and document metadata (not the
# documents themselves, which are SQLite files under GRIST_DATA_DIR). The
# image points it at a SQLite file on the /persist volume; switch the whole
# block to Postgres only if you are also giving Grist a Postgres to talk to.

# Driver. Empty means "sqlite" (app/server/lib/dbUtils.ts); "postgres" is the
# other supported value.
# @type=enum(sqlite, postgres)
TYPEORM_TYPE=

# SQLite file path, or the Postgres database name. The image bakes the path on
# the persistent volume; changing it strands the existing accounts.
TYPEORM_DATABASE=/persist/home.sqlite3

# Postgres connection details. Ignored for SQLite.
TYPEORM_HOST=
# @type=port
TYPEORM_PORT=
TYPEORM_USERNAME=
# @sensitive
TYPEORM_PASSWORD=
# Extra TypeORM connection options as a JSON object, merged over the rest.
TYPEORM_EXTRA=
# TypeORM connection name; defaults to "default".
TYPEORM_NAME=
# Log every query. Very noisy; for debugging only.
# @type=boolean
TYPEORM_LOGGING=
# Log queries slower than this many milliseconds.
# @type=number
TYPEORM_LOG_SLOW_MS=
# Redis URL for TypeORM's own query cache, if you want it separate from
# REDIS_URL.
# @sensitive
TYPEORM_REDIS_URL=

# Use prepared statements against Postgres. Turn off for poolers (PgBouncer in
# transaction mode) that cannot keep them.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_POSTGRES_USE_PREPARED_STATEMENTS=

# ─── Documents on disk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Directory holding the .grist document files. The image bakes /persist/docs,
# which is inside the compose's grist-persist volume. Move it off the volume
# and documents do not survive a container restart.
GRIST_DATA_DIR=/persist/docs

# Instance config directory (config.json, generated keys). Also on the
# persistent volume in the image.
GRIST_INST_DIR=/persist

# SQLite durability mode for documents: "wal" for write-ahead logging, "sync"
# for SYNCHRONOUS=full. Empty keeps SQLite's default.
# @type=enum(wal, sync)
# @docs("SQLite WAL mode", https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html)
GRIST_SQLITE_MODE=

# Seconds to wait after a document changes before taking a backup. Defaults
# to 15.
# @type=number
GRIST_BACKUP_DELAY_SECS=

# Number of recent snapshots always retained per document, before the bucketed
# rules apply. Defaults to 5.
# @type=number
GRIST_SNAPSHOT_KEEP=

# JSON object capping how many snapshots each time bucket keeps, e.g.
# {"hour": 25, "day": 32, "isoWeek": 12, "month": 96, "year": 1000}.
GRIST_SNAPSHOT_TIME_CAP=

# ─── External storage and attachments ──────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("How do I set up external attachment storage?", https://support.getgrist.com/self-managed/#how-do-i-set-up-external-attachment-storage)

# Where large attachments live. The code's default is "snapshots" (external
# store, which only actually engages once snapshot storage is configured;
# otherwise Grist logs a warning and keeps attachments in the document).
# "test" is a temp-filesystem store for tests. Despite the README, "none" is
# NOT accepted at this version and makes the server throw
# UnsupportedExternalAttachmentsMode.
# @type=enum(snapshots, test)
GRIST_EXTERNAL_ATTACHMENTS_MODE=snapshots

# Per-document attachment total, in MB, beyond which Grist recommends moving
# attachments to external storage. Defaults to 50. (The README spells this
# GRIST_ATTACHMENT_THRESHOLD_MB, singular, which the code never reads.)
# @type=number
GRIST_ATTACHMENTS_THRESHOLD_MB=

# Hard cap on bytes of attachments kept inside a document.
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_INTERNAL_ATTACHMENTS_BYTES=

# S3-compatible (MinIO) object storage for document snapshots and external
# attachments. All of these are read together; the bucket is what switches the
# backend on.
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_BUCKET=
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_BUCKET_REGION=
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_PREFIX=
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_ENDPOINT=
# @type=port
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_PORT=
# @type=boolean
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_USE_SSL=
# @sensitive
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=
# @sensitive
GRIST_DOCS_MINIO_SECRET_KEY=

# Filesystem-backed implementation of the external-storage interface. Added in
# 1.7.14 for tests; not a supported production backend.
GRIST_FS_STORAGE_DIR=

# Force the S3/snapshot storage backend off even when it is configured.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_DISABLE_S3=

# ─── Formula sandbox ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("Sandboxing (v1.7.18 README)", https://github.com/gristlabs/grist-core/blob/v1.7.18/README.md#sandboxing)

# Which sandbox runs document formulas. The compose sets "gvisor", the
# strongest option the image ships; the entrypoint probes it at startup and
# refuses to boot if it fails, rather than silently downgrading. "unsandboxed"
# and "skip" run Python straight on the host process with no protection at
# all, so a formula author then has the container's privileges.
# @type=enum(gvisor, pyodide, unsandboxed, skip, docker, macSandboxExec, sandboxed)
GRIST_SANDBOX_FLAVOR=gvisor

# Program or image the chosen flavor runs, when you need to override it (a
# python path for unsandboxed, an image name for docker, a run.py path for
# gvisor). Empty uses the image's own.
GRIST_SANDBOX=

# Flags passed to runsc. The image bakes "-unprivileged -ignore-cgroups",
# which is what makes gvisor work inside an unprivileged container; clearing
# it will usually make the startup gvisor check fail.
GVISOR_FLAGS=-unprivileged -ignore-cgroups

# Extra arguments appended to the sandbox command line.
GRIST_SANDBOX_APPEND_ARGS=

# oom_score_adj applied to the sandbox process, so the kernel kills a runaway
# formula before it kills Grist.
# @type=number
GRIST_SANDBOX_OOM_SCORE_ADJ=

# gvisor checkpoint/restore of a warmed Python interpreter, for faster
# document opens. The image manages this itself at startup.
GRIST_CHECKPOINT=
GRIST_CHECKPOINT_MAKE=

# Skip Deno when running the pyodide sandbox flavor.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_PYODIDE_SKIP_DENO=

# Throttle sandbox CPU usage.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_THROTTLE_CPU=

# ─── Outbound requests: webhooks, REQUEST(), imports ───────────────────────
# @docs("Webhooks", https://support.getgrist.com/webhooks/)

# Comma-separated allowlist of domains a webhook may target, e.g.
# "webhook.site,zapier.com". Empty means no webhook targets are permitted.
# "*" allows everything, which lets any document editor make this server issue
# requests to your internal network. Pair it with
# GRIST_PROXY_FOR_UNTRUSTED_URLS if you use it.
ALLOWED_WEBHOOK_DOMAINS=

# Proxy that all user-triggered outbound requests (webhooks, REQUEST(), import
# from URL) are sent through. The literal "direct" (the default) sends them
# straight out from the container. A locked-down proxy here is what keeps
# document editors from reaching internal addresses.
GRIST_PROXY_FOR_UNTRUSTED_URLS=

# Deprecated spelling of GRIST_PROXY_FOR_UNTRUSTED_URLS; still read, and it
# logs a warning telling you to migrate.
GRIST_HTTPS_PROXY=

# Corporate proxy used for Grist's OWN trusted fetches: the custom widget
# manifest and the OIDC issuer's discovery document.
HTTPS_PROXY=

# Enables the REQUEST() formula function, which performs HTTP requests from
# the sandbox. Off by default: on a publicly reachable server it lets any
# formula author probe your internal network.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("REQUEST function", https://support.getgrist.com/functions/#request)
GRIST_ENABLE_REQUEST_FUNCTION=

# Milliseconds between webhook delivery attempts (default 1000) and how many
# attempts before a webhook payload is dropped (default 20).
# @type=number
GRIST_TRIGGER_WAIT_DELAY=
# @type=number
GRIST_TRIGGER_MAX_ATTEMPTS=

# Longest a queue of undelivered webhook payloads may grow before Grist starts
# discarding them.
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_QUEUE_SIZE=

# ─── OIDC single sign-on ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Setting GRIST_OIDC_IDP_ISSUER is what switches Grist from the passwordless
# fallback login to a real identity provider. Everything below is inert until
# it is set.
# @docs("OpenID Connect", https://support.getgrist.com/install/oidc/)

# Issuer URL; Grist fetches /.well-known/openid-configuration from it.
# @type=url
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_ISSUER=
# Client credentials for this Grist instance, from the IdP.
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_CLIENT_ID=
# @sensitive
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Public origin of Grist as the IdP knows it, used to build the redirect URI.
# Defaults to APP_HOME_URL.
# @type=url
GRIST_OIDC_SP_HOST=
# Space-separated scopes. Defaults to "openid email profile".
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_SCOPES=
# Claim to read the display name from. Empty uses "name", or
# given_name + family_name.
GRIST_OIDC_SP_PROFILE_NAME_ATTR=
# Claim to read the email from. Defaults to "email".
GRIST_OIDC_SP_PROFILE_EMAIL_ATTR=
# Accept an identity whose email_verified claim is false. Only for IdPs that
# never set it; otherwise it accepts unverified addresses.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_OIDC_SP_IGNORE_EMAIL_VERIFIED=
# Comma-separated protections on the auth request. Defaults to "PKCE,STATE";
# also accepts NONCE. Removing PKCE or STATE weakens the flow.
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_ENABLED_PROTECTIONS=
# RP-initiated logout endpoint, when discovery does not advertise one.
# @type=url
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_END_SESSION_ENDPOINT=
# Do not call the end-session endpoint on logout (some IdPs mishandle it).
# @type=boolean
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_SKIP_END_SESSION_ENDPOINT=
# acr_values to request.
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_ACR_VALUES=
# JSON object of extra client metadata passed to the oidc-client library.
GRIST_OIDC_IDP_EXTRA_CLIENT_METADATA=
# Seconds before an HTTP call to the IdP times out; 0 disables the timeout.
# @type=number
GRIST_OIDC_SP_HTTP_TIMEOUT=
# Comma-separated extra IdP claims to persist on the user record
# (options.ssoExtraInfo), e.g. "onekey,anotherkey".
GRIST_IDP_EXTRA_PROPS=

# ─── SAML single sign-on ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("SAML", https://support.getgrist.com/install/saml/)

# Public origin of Grist as the IdP knows it, used to build ACS/metadata URLs.
# @type=url
GRIST_SAML_SP_HOST=
# Paths, inside the container, to this service provider's private key and
# certificate. Mount them; the key is a secret even though this is a path.
GRIST_SAML_SP_KEY=
GRIST_SAML_SP_CERT=
# IdP SSO and SLO endpoints.
# @type=url
GRIST_SAML_IDP_LOGIN=
# @type=url
GRIST_SAML_IDP_LOGOUT=
# Skip single logout at the IdP.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SAML_IDP_SKIP_SLO=
# IdP signing certificate(s) used to verify assertions.
GRIST_SAML_IDP_CERTS=
# Accept unencrypted assertions. Only over a channel you already trust.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SAML_IDP_UNENCRYPTED=

# ─── Forward (proxy) authentication ────────────────────────────────────────
# For deployments where an authenticating proxy in front of Grist has already
# established who the user is. Setting the header name is what activates it.
# The proxy MUST strip this header from inbound client requests, or anyone can
# claim any identity by sending it themselves.

# Request header carrying the authenticated user's email, e.g.
# X-Forwarded-User.
GRIST_FORWARD_AUTH_HEADER=
# Deprecated synonym of GRIST_FORWARD_AUTH_HEADER, still read.
GRIST_PROXY_AUTH_HEADER=
# Path Grist sends unauthenticated visitors to, for the proxy to intercept.
# Defaults to /auth/login.
GRIST_FORWARD_AUTH_LOGIN_PATH=
# Path Grist sends logout through. Empty means logout is handled by Grist.
GRIST_FORWARD_AUTH_LOGOUT_PATH=

# ─── Custom widgets and plugins ────────────────────────────────────────────
# @docs("Custom widgets", https://support.getgrist.com/widget-custom/)

# Manifest listing the custom widgets offered in the picker. Defaults to the
# grist-widget repo's published manifest; point it at your own to serve
# widgets offline.
# @type=url
GRIST_WIDGET_LIST_URL=
# Tolerate a GRIST_WIDGET_LIST_URL that cannot be fetched, instead of failing.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_WIDGET_LIST_URL_OPTIONAL=
# Ignore the widgets bundled into the image via NPM packages.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_SKIP_BUNDLED_WIDGETS=
# Serve plugins from the app's own host instead of a separate one. That hands
# plugin code the app's cookies; only for setups where you control every
# plugin.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_TRUST_PLUGINS=
# Port to serve untrusted plugin content on, as an alternative to
# APP_UNTRUSTED_URL.
# @type=port
GRIST_UNTRUSTED_PORT=
# Comma-separated widget URLs allowed to be embedded beyond the manifest.
PERMITTED_CUSTOM_WIDGETS=
# Enable plugins still marked experimental.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_EXPERIMENTAL_PLUGINS=
# Extra directory scanned for plugins, at $GRIST_USER_ROOT/plugins.
GRIST_USER_ROOT=
# Additional directory of plugin code.
GRIST_PLUGIN_PATH=

# ─── AI assistant ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The formula assistant is off until an API key is present. Everything typed
# into the assistant, plus document structure, is sent to the endpoint below.
# @docs("AI Assistant", https://support.getgrist.com/ai-assistant/)

# API key for the chat-completion endpoint. OPENAI_API_KEY is read as a
# fallback; ASSISTANT_API_KEY wins when both are set.
# @sensitive
ASSISTANT_API_KEY=
# @sensitive
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OpenAI-compatible chat-completions URL. Empty uses OpenAI; set it to point
# at a self-hosted model instead.
# @type=url
ASSISTANT_CHAT_COMPLETION_ENDPOINT=
# Model name, and the model used when the context does not fit the first one.
ASSISTANT_MODEL=
ASSISTANT_LONGER_CONTEXT_MODEL=
# Cap on tokens per completion.
# @type=number
ASSISTANT_MAX_TOKENS=
# Cap on tool calls in one assistant turn.
# @type=number
ASSISTANT_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=
# Request structured output from the model. Defaults to false.
# @type=boolean
ASSISTANT_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT=

# ─── Limits and timeouts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Max size in MB for an uploaded attachment, and for an imported file. Empty
# or 0 means unlimited.
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_UPLOAD_ATTACHMENT_MB=
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_UPLOAD_IMPORT_MB=

# Concurrent API requests allowed against one document. Defaults to 10;
# 0 is unlimited.
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_PARALLEL_REQUESTS_PER_DOC=

# Seconds a document stays loaded in memory after the last client leaves.
# Defaults to 30 when NODE_ENV=production (as the image sets), else 5. Higher
# means faster reopens and more memory held.
# @type=number
GRIST_ACTIVEDOC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=

# Milliseconds a client has to accept a broadcast before being disconnected.
# Defaults to 60000.
# @type=number
GRIST_BROADCAST_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Milliseconds a user-supplied SQL query may run for. Defaults to 1000.
# @type=number
GRIST_SQL_TIMEOUT_MSEC=

# Node HTTP server timeouts, in milliseconds. Raise them for very long uploads
# or downloads through a slow link.
# @type=number
GRIST_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=
# @type=number
GRIST_KEEP_ALIVE_TIMEOUT_MS=
# @type=number
GRIST_HEADERS_TIMEOUT_MS=

# ActionHistory pruning thresholds (rows, then bytes; a 1.25 grace factor
# applies). Defaults are 1000 rows and 1GB. Setting these too low breaks the
# "Work on a copy" feature.
# @type=number
GRIST_ACTION_HISTORY_MAX_ROWS=
# @type=number
GRIST_ACTION_HISTORY_MAX_BYTES=

# Memory ceiling for a doc worker, and the cgroup files it reads current usage
# from. Only useful in a multi-worker deployment.
# @type=number
GRIST_DOC_WORKER_MAX_MEMORY_MB=
GRIST_DOC_WORKER_MAX_MEMORY_BYTES_PATH=
GRIST_DOC_WORKER_USED_MEMORY_BYTES_PATH=

# Per-org caps used by hosted deployments.
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_NEW_USER_INVITES_PER_ORG=
# @type=number
GRIST_MAX_BILLING_MANAGERS_PER_ORG=

# ─── Interface customization ───────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated UI parts to force on, and to hide. Allowed names:
# helpCenter, billing, templates, createSite, multiSite, multiAccounts,
# importFromAirtable, sendToDrive, tutorials, supportGrist, themes,
# automations. HIDE wins over UI_FEATURES for any part in both.
GRIST_UI_FEATURES=
GRIST_HIDE_UI_ELEMENTS=

# Org "domain" whose public documents are offered as templates.
GRIST_TEMPLATE_ORG=

# Live cursors and presence avatars. Enabled by default; "false" turns all
# presence features off. The cap is 1-99 users, default 99.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ENABLE_USER_PRESENCE=
# @type=number
GRIST_USER_PRESENCE_MAX_USERS=
# @type=boolean
GRIST_USER_PRESENCE_ICON_PER_TAB=

# Links shown in the UI. Empty uses Grist's own; point them at your own help
# desk for an internal deployment.
# @type=url
GRIST_HELP_CENTER=
# @type=url
GRIST_TERMS_OF_SERVICE_URL=
# @type=url
GRIST_CONTACT_SUPPORT_URL=
# @type=url
FREE_COACHING_CALL_URL=
# YouTube video id shown on the home page and during onboarding.
GRIST_ONBOARDING_VIDEO_ID=
# JSON object overriding any subset of the ICommonUrls interface at once.
GRIST_CUSTOM_COMMON_URLS=

# Image used when a Grist link is unfurled in chat or on social media.
# @type=url
GRIST_OPEN_GRAPH_PREVIEW_IMAGE=

# Serve custom.css (from APP_STATIC_URL) on every page.
# @type=boolean
APP_STATIC_INCLUDE_CUSTOM_CSS=

# Loads this URL in a <script> tag on every app page. It runs with full access
# to the Grist app origin, so it can read anything the signed-in user can.
# @type=url
GRIST_INCLUDE_CUSTOM_SCRIPT_URL=

# Warn a user before they share a document publicly.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_WARN_BEFORE_SHARING_PUBLICLY=

# Extra words the data engine should treat as truthy/falsy beyond the English
# defaults, comma-separated, e.g. "oui,ja,si".
GRIST_TRUTHY_VALUES=
GRIST_FALSY_VALUES=

# Border added around rendered forms for security. "border" (default) or
# "minimal".
# @type=enum(border, minimal)
GRIST_FEATURE_FORM_FRAMING=

# Directory of translation files, if you ship your own.
GRIST_LOCALES_DIR=

# ─── API surface ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Enables the experimental SCIM user-provisioning endpoint. It exposes user
# management to whoever holds an admin API key.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("SCIM API", https://support.getgrist.com/install/scim/)
GRIST_ENABLE_SCIM=
# Email SCIM operations are attributed to.
# @type=email
GRIST_SCIM_EMAIL=

# Enables service accounts: scoped API keys a user can mint for automations.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ENABLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNTS=

# Enables the Model Context Protocol endpoint, letting an AI client drive
# documents through the API. Grant it deliberately.
# @type=boolean
# @docs("Connected apps", https://support.getgrist.com/connected-apps/)
GRIST_MCP_ENABLED=

# Re-enables the deprecated DELETE /api/orgs/:orgId endpoint.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ALLOW_DEPRECATED_BARE_ORG_DELETE=

# ─── Google Drive integration ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers "Import from Google Drive" and "Send to Google Drive". All three come
# from a Google Cloud project you own; leaving them empty hides the feature.

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# @sensitive
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# @sensitive
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# OAuth scope requested. Defaults to drive.file, which limits Grist to files
# it created or the user explicitly picked.
GOOGLE_DRIVE_SCOPE=

# ─── Telemetry, updates and logging ────────────────────────────────────────

# How much usage data is sent to Grist Labs: off (the default), limited, or
# full. Set here, it overrides whatever the Admin Panel says.
# @type=enum(off, limited, full)
# @docs("Telemetry", https://support.getgrist.com/telemetry/)
GRIST_TELEMETRY_LEVEL=

# Whether Grist may phone home to check for a newer release. The official
# gristlabs/grist image builds with this on; "false" stops the check.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_ALLOW_AUTOMATIC_VERSION_CHECKING=

# Base URL the in-place "switch to the full edition" upgrade (added 1.7.17)
# downloads extensions from. The image bakes Grist's own; point it at a mirror
# for an air-gapped install.
# @type=url
GRIST_EXT_FULL_EDITION_BASE_URL=

# Minimum log level. Defaults to "debug", which is verbose; "info" or "warn"
# is usually what you want on a server.
# @type=enum(error, warn, info, debug)
GRIST_LOG_LEVEL=

# Emit log lines as JSON instead of plain text.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_LOG_AS_JSON=

# Log HTTP requests and responses, and (with the first also on) their bodies.
# The body log can leak document contents and credentials into your logs.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_LOG_HTTP=
# @type=boolean
GRIST_LOG_HTTP_BODY=
# Comma-separated request paths to leave out of the HTTP log.
GRIST_LOG_SKIP_HTTP=

# Log the details of every API call.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_LOG_API_DETAILS=

# If set, Prometheus metrics are served on this port. It carries no
# authentication, so do not publish it.
# @type=port
GRIST_PROMCLIENT_PORT=

# ─── Multi-server deployment ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of this applies to the single container this template runs; it is here
# because these are the knobs that appear the moment you add a second one.

# Route clients to whichever peer holds the document, so every server can be
# deployed identically behind a load balancer. Requires an Enterprise
# activation key, and refuses to start alongside APP_DOC_URL.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_FLEET=
# Stable identity of this doc worker. Two servers sharing a value can open the
# same document at once and corrupt it. Leave empty to have one derived.
GRIST_DOC_WORKER_ID=
# Group a worker belongs to, for assignment.
GRIST_WORKER_GROUP=
# How many doc workers the deployment expects.
# @type=number
DOC_WORKER_COUNT=
# API a server registers and deregisters itself with, at a load balancer.
# @type=url
GRIST_ROUTER_URL=
# Assume a 404 from a doc worker URL means that worker is gone.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_MANAGED_WORKERS=
# Experimental worker-assignment strategy.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_EXPERIMENTAL_WORKER_ASSIGNMENT=

# Forces the full (Enterprise) edition on regardless of what the home database
# records. Since 1.7.18 the edition itself lives in the DB as
# GRIST_SERVER_EDITION; this env var still takes precedence.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_FORCE_ENABLE_ENTERPRISE=
# The recorded edition, normally managed from the Admin Panel rather than set
# here.
# @type=enum(community, full)
GRIST_SERVER_EDITION=

# ─── Container runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The image runs in production mode, which lengthens document timeouts and
# lets Express skip development-only work. Setting "development" on a deployed
# instance makes it slower and more talkative, not safer.
# @type=enum(production, development)
NODE_ENV=production

# Node flags. The image bakes --no-deprecation to silence a punycode warning
# that is only relevant to Grist's own developers; replacing the value drops
# that suppression.
NODE_OPTIONS=--no-deprecation

# Extra module resolution paths. The container's start command sets this
# itself (_build:_build/ext:_build/stubs:ext/node_modules); overriding it
# breaks the boot.
NODE_PATH=

# Unprivileged user and group the entrypoint drops to after fixing ownership
# of /persist. Baked into the image; change both together or the container
# runs as root.
GRIST_DOCKER_USER=grist
GRIST_DOCKER_GROUP=grist

# Restart in place to apply configuration changes without dropping the
# listening socket. On by default for Linux under Node, which is this image.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_RESTART_SHELL=

# Set when Grist is started by an external supervisor that owns restarts.
# @type=boolean
GRIST_RUNNING_UNDER_SUPERVISOR=

# Extra directories of Enterprise/extension code and static assets, populated
# by the image itself.
GRIST_EXT_DIR=
GRIST_STATIC_EXT_DIR=
